      "side": 1,
      "message": "So these are copied into the freetype directory directly, which seems a bit awkward. FreeType already has a top level `builds/` directory which is a lot like this, with various customizations like this. Of course, these are generally applied at configure time, which would be like applying these patches directly with `git_repository`\u0027s `patches` attribute. However, we want to pick between these at build time and bazel doesn\u0027t really have a separate \"configure\" phase like that.\n\nIn any event, I wish there were a better way to do this but I\u0027m not seeing one at the moment. If we do this I would prefer that the includes be copied to `builds/skia/no-type1` and `builds/skia/android`. Failing that, `include/skia/no-type1` or something like that so that it\u0027s obvious that Skia\u0027s build is the one dropping these in there.",
      "revId": "bea460211babef921b4326ee0cb2ec21fdee755c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
