      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T17:22:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had considered `git_repository`\u0027s `patches` attribute but that doesn\u0027t work for 2 reasons: 1) We use git-sync-deps to download the repos (currently) and 2) It seemed a bit awkward to store file content in a patch-format instead of the file itself.\n\nAt some point we\u0027ll stop doing 1), but even then 2) feels a bit cumbersome.\n\nI just tried `builds/skia/...`, but that ran into the strip prefix issue I was seeing before, so I had to go with `include/skia/...`",
